{"name":"Locust","hex":"#a2a580","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Locust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Locust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Locust","blocks":[{"text":"Locusts are various species of short-horned grasshoppers in the family Acrididae that have a swarming phase. These insects are usually solitary, but under certain circumstances they become more abundant and change their behaviour and habits, becoming gregarious. No taxonomic distinction is made between locust and grasshopper species; the basis for the definition is whether a species forms swarms under intermittently suitable conditions. Swarming has evolved independently in multiple lineages, comprising at least 18 genera in 5 different subfamilies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Locusta-migratoria-wanderheuschrecke.jpg/330px-Locusta-migratoria-wanderheuschrecke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust","wikidata":"Q83931"},{"title":"Locust (Gears of War)","blocks":[{"text":"The Locust are a fictional collective of subterranean species in the Gears of War media franchise. Created by Epic Games, they were introduced in the 2006 video game Gears of War as the principal enemy faction opposing humanity. Their organized military, commonly called the Locust Horde, emerges from beneath the surface of the planet Sera during Emergence Day and wages a prolonged war against the human Coalition of Ordered Governments (COG). Led by the human Queen Myrrah and Locust commanders like General RAAM and Skorge, the Locust are depicted as the principal antagonistic force of the Gears of War franchise."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/20/MyrrahLocust.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locust_(Gears_of_War)","wikidata":"Q5978313"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/CSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/CSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg/1280px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/CSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Millions of swarming Australian plague locusts on the move","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACSIRO_ScienceImage_7007_Plague_locusts_on_the_move.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Copulating_desert_locust_pair.jpg/500px-Copulating_desert_locust_pair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Copulating_desert_locust_pair.jpg/500px-Copulating_desert_locust_pair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Desert locusts in copulation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACopulating_desert_locust_pair.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/DesertLocust.jpeg/330px-DesertLocust.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/DesertLocust.jpeg/330px-DesertLocust.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Solitaria (grasshopper) and gregaria (swarming) phases of the desert locust","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADese